>> title: Castella
>> category: Cakes & Loaves
>> tags: honey, sponge, japanese, oven
>> counters: Bakery
>> aka: kasutera, カステラ, honey castella, honey sponge cake
>> servings: 8
>> time: 1 hr 15 min
>> slack: unforgiving — the foam is whipped to the ribbon and then baked low and slow, and it is the one cake on the shelf where a slammed oven door genuinely deflates it; the batter is also poured from a height and the bubbles struck out on purpose, because a bubble left in bakes as a hole

Line a #9x5-in loaf pan{} with parchment.

Preheat the #oven{} to 320°F (160°C).

Whisk @honey{2%Tbs}(40 g), @warm water{2%Tbs}(30 mL), @mirin{1%tsp}(5 mL).

Beat @eggs{4%large}, @granulated sugar{3/4%cup}(150 g) over warm water to the ribbon stage.

Whisk @&(3)honey syrup{} into @&(~1)egg foam{}.

Fold @bread flour{1%cup}(125 g; sifted twice) into @&(~1)batter{}.

Bake @&(~1)batter{} at 320°F for ~{45%min}.
